{"id": "EUVD-2026-86226", "enisaUuid": "9a0c7318-cdee-36c6-863b-bc78439565f7", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nstaging: media: tegra-video: fix of_node_put() on VIP parse errors\n\ntegra_vip_channel_of_parse() initializes np from dev->of_node without\ntaking a reference, but its error paths drop one through the\nerr_node_put label. This underflows the refcount of the VIP device's\nOF node when endpoint parsing fails on a malformed device tree.\n\nThe only reference the function takes on np is the success-path\nof_node_get() stored in vip->chan.of_node, and that one is already\nreleased by the tegra_vip_init() error path and by tegra_vip_exit().\n\nReturn errors directly instead of jumping to the bogus cleanup label.", "datePublished": "2026-09-24T15:21:06", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:07:34", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a3783800c9475fa58b8db0885893f96a23f949da", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1295ba29ac590bbb5c4a586afd408018168af10b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/656d047dc0c29c0964d840217a0593f16aa9bc5e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fc9937019cf7e2fe4e29f9341e6400bcd2cde721", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7393372f79db940acff206b43e2905685a0c57ad"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-93223", "GHSA-f6j6-qc9x-24h7"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "067751f1-6ee3-3b01-8738-8ddc7b2f3062", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.4"}, {"id": "1861cb94-285f-3060-aa60-3942bbbec489", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.157"}, {"id": "19859bfe-f1ff-3963-ac38-535bcfde4b10", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.50"}, {"id": "2c9fc1d6-54de-3efe-b0e4-b4f3ccd825f8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e740d199cf0ff1e53ddc2ab067c0a09b55845d68 <1295ba29ac590bbb5c4a586afd408018168af10b"}, {"id": "36a67b96-ada4-3f82-8688-9fba2c56cf4b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.109"}, {"id": "7a950761-373c-3b54-9d8b-afe9d3aef505", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e740d199cf0ff1e53ddc2ab067c0a09b55845d68 <7393372f79db940acff206b43e2905685a0c57ad"}, {"id": "80ce20cb-b36a-37ec-82a2-86b80db1ada3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e740d199cf0ff1e53ddc2ab067c0a09b55845d68 <656d047dc0c29c0964d840217a0593f16aa9bc5e"}, {"id": "810b763b-4e55-3bb8-bc1b-18a76836f8c2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "8a70f8ff-4655-3a27-99b9-8fc86d1a0769", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.5"}, {"id": "a6f5070f-729e-34bc-8c85-8418ca2090cb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "bf7f0260-5f38-3baa-8794-85ea92d6585c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e740d199cf0ff1e53ddc2ab067c0a09b55845d68 <a3783800c9475fa58b8db0885893f96a23f949da"}, {"id": "cf87b03e-4790-3821-85e0-8f80a83507f6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e740d199cf0ff1e53ddc2ab067c0a09b55845d68 <fc9937019cf7e2fe4e29f9341e6400bcd2cde721"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "e880aacb-2828-31c3-afa8-64617174c6e0", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}